    {
      "name": "overview_contribution",
      "pass": true,
      "text": "THE RESEARCH QUESTION\n\nCan uncertainty guide the search for useful crystals?\n\nExplicit predictive uncertainty during symmetry-constrained generation may improve stable, novel crystal discovery in underrepresented chemical spaces.\n\nOur contribution is the decision and evaluation pipeline. Around pretrained CrystalFormer and CHGNet, we built calibrated uncertainty and diversity-based selection, controlled comparisons on held-out chemical systems, strict candidate screening and a traceable record of model and first-principles checks. This makes the discovery hypothesis measurable within a limited compute budget.\n\nExplore what we built \u00e2\u2020\u2019",
      "recorded_at": "2026-10-22T17:00:07.124Z"
    },
